  "unmanaged_keys_note": "Keys that live in .env.example and have NO manifest entry, so env-example-guard never compares them. Recorded 2026-09-06 while verifying CD-1: the guard iterated the manifest and asked 'does the file agree?', never the reverse, so 88 of 219 keys were invisible to it -- including VODOU_FS_TOOLS_UNSANDBOXED, the line that turns filesystem confinement OFF and ships active. This list is a RATCHET, not an allowlist: the guard fails when it GROWS. Adding a key to .env.example means adding a manifest entry; putting one here instead is a deliberate, reviewable choice. The list should shrink. 2026-09-06: the three VODOU_FS_TOOLS_* keys moved OUT of this list and into the SYSTEM section as part of CD-1. Whole-machine file access is a decided default, so its value now has a guard behind it rather than being unmanaged by accident. 88 -> 85."
}
